PASS M1 gateway-style import registers /events when KANBAN_GANTT_WS=1 — ['/boards', '/gantt', '/tasks/bulk', '/tasks/{task_id}', '/tasks/{task_id}/status', '/tasks/{task_id}/comments', '/tasks/{task_id}/assignee', '/projects', '/profiles', '/tasks', '/tasks/{task_id}/parent', '/tasks/{task_id}/parent/{parent_id}', '/meta', '/events']
PASS M2 the websocket module is the one the plugin router uses — loaded|same-instance
PASS M3 flag off ⇒ no /events route, REST route set unchanged — [... '/meta']  (no '/events')
PASS M4 flag off ⇒ the websocket module is still importable (no crash) — loaded|same-instance

RESULT: 4/4 checks passed
```

## 3. After the fix — the probe against the live gateway, with the real token

```
PASS G1 unauthenticated upgrade refused — InvalidStatus
PASS G2 gateway accepts the upgrade and pushes a snapshot first — type=snapshot version=1 tasks=22 bytes=10494
PASS G3 out-of-process writes are pushed over the gateway socket — latencies_ms=[553, 554, 555] versions=[2, 3, 4]
PASS G4 a second subscriber is accepted on the same board — version=5
PASS G5 unknown board refused (no crash, no frame) — InvalidStatus

GATEWAY RESULT: 5/5 checks passed
```

(An earlier run of the same probe, one subscriber, gave `latencies_ms=[554, 553, 553]`,
`tasks=19 bytes=9516`; the board grows as the probe inserts its own tasks.)

## 4. Gateway log — the mount and the auth gate

`$SANDBOX/home/logs/{agent,gui,errors}.log`, filtered:

```
INFO hermes_cli.web_server: Mounted plugin API routes: /api/plugins/kanban-gantt/
INFO kanban_gantt_plugin_ws: kanban-gantt ws: rejected upgrade (core_reject)
INFO kanban_gantt_plugin_ws: kanban-gantt ws: stream for wsgw ended: RuntimeError
WARNING hermes_cli.plugins: Failed to load plugin 'kanban-gantt': No __init__.py in …/plugins/kanban-gantt
```

* the mount is the production one (`include_router` + `_plugin_route_secret_scope`), not the
  plugin's standalone `create_app()`;
* a bad/absent credential is a **`core_reject`** — `authorize()` did delegate to core
  `_ws_auth_ok`; the line records the reason, never the credential;
* **`?token=` redaction**: `grep -i token` over every gateway log (and the redirected stdout)
  matches **nothing**, and this deployment emits **no uvicorn access log** — the concern is
  closed by measurement;
* `stream for wsgw ended: RuntimeError` fires on every last-subscriber disconnect (benign so
  far: the next subscriber recreates the stream) — carried as a T1 teardown item;
* the `No __init__.py` warning is a sandbox-copy artifact (the harness copies only
  `dashboard/` + `plugin.yaml`); it did not prevent the REST or ws routes from mounting, and
  the real plugin ships `__init__.py`.

## 5. The pinning trap, reproduced end-to-end (hard part #2)

The gateway launched from a kanban worker's shell inherits the worker's env, including
`HERMES_KANBAN_DB=/…/boards/gantt-demo/kanban.db`. In that (first) run:

```
PASS G2 gateway accepts the upgrade and pushes a snapshot first — … tasks=20 bytes=10383
FAIL G3 write 0 pushed a frame — no frame within 8 s
FAIL G5 unknown board refused (no crash, no frame) — got a frame
GATEWAY RESULT: 3/7 checks passed
```

i.e. `?board=does-not-exist` was served a valid snapshot, and writes to the intended board
were never seen, because every subscription resolved to the *pinned* board instead of the
requested slug. Same behaviour from a plain shell with the pinned env:

```
khome /home/blavenie/.hermes/cache/scratch/ws-gw-probe/kh
wsgw           -> /home/blavenie/.hermes/kanban/boards/gantt-demo/kanban.db True
does-not-exist -> /home/blavenie/.hermes/kanban/boards/gantt-demo/kanban.db True
```

Mitigation today: start the gateway env-clean (`env -u HERMES_KANBAN_DB -u HERMES_KANBAN_BOARD`).
Proper fix (T1): after resolving a slug, assert the path is `<boards_root>/<slug>/kanban.db`
and refuse anything else.
